          "claim": "Under [A1], in the standard genus-one splitting, remove an open tubular neighborhood of the $(2,3)$ curve from the splitting torus and take the two remaining solid-torus pieces. Their intersection is an annulus $A$. The product cell structures on the solid tori collapse their disk fibers to core circles $a$ and $b$, while the annulus collapses along its interval factor to its core. These product collapses retain the common core and give the based homotopy-pushout spine with one vertex, edges $a,b$, and one $2$-cell recording equality of the two images of the annulus core. The core winds twice around the first solid-torus core and three times around the second, so its attaching word is $a^2b^{-3}$. The collapses of the product disk fibers and annular interval are elementary cell collapses, giving the stated simple-spine certificate, not merely an abstract group presentation.",
